# Task delivery

Authoritative: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), [docs/features/](../../docs/features/), [docs/00-status.md](../../docs/00-status.md).

## Lifecycle

Understand → Plan → Implement → Validate → Review. Persist significant decisions in docs/ADRs, not only chat.

## Scope

- Stay inside the task’s allowed paths; report exceptions before expanding.
- Default forbidden: `Packages/manifest.json`, silent `ProjectSettings/**` edits, secrets, store publish.
- Do not expand into unrelated systems “while here.”

## Design ownership

- Approved GDD / architecture / feature acceptance / ADRs are intent — do not silently rewrite them to match code.
- Status docs and implementation notes may be updated after verified changes.
- On conflict with approved design: escalate with options.

## Definition of Done

- [ ] Acceptance criteria met or exceptions listed
- [ ] Compiles on the project’s pinned Unity version (`ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt`)
- [ ] Relevant automated tests executed (or blocked reason + manual alternative)
- [ ] Scene/prefab diffs reviewed if assets changed
- [ ] Docs/ADR updated when behavior or architecture changes
- [ ] Completion report per AGENTS.md

## Human approval required

Core gameplay/feel changes, package or Unity upgrades, release/store actions, bulk scene rewrites, new third-party dependencies.
